  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nConfidence is increase in accumulating snowfall this Friday and\nSaturday. A low pressure center is expected to cross into the\nOhio Valley Wednesday night bringing some showers to the region\nthrough the day on Thursday. Probabilities continue to show a\ntrend of 40% to 60% of exceeding 0.50\". The frontal passage is\nexpected to occur by 06Z Friday with much of the precip changing\nto snow showers with Lake Enhanced snowfall expected. \n\nCurrently, the NBM as well as other ensembles, suggest some\naccumulating snowfall over the WV ridges. In fact the \nprobabilities show a strong 80% to 90% potential of exceeding\n3\". While the potential of reaching winter storm criteria is a\nless than 20% probability. Still, there are still a couple\nfactors to take into place concerning the confidence. Here are\nthe 2 scenarios possible:\n\n1. The expected flow aloft could make for a more progressive\nsystem and a quicker passage through the area. This would be due\nto a more southern passage and would result in little to no snow\nin the lower terrain and less than Advisory criteria for the WV\nmountains. \n\n2. A slower system passing through the the area a bit more north\nwould produce a scenario closer to the outcome described above.\nThis would bring advisory snow to the WV mountains and\npotentially the northern counties but the northern counties \nreaching advisory criteria is a 10% to 20% probability. The only\nother concern would be the small potential of the WV Mountains\nreceiving warning criteria. At this time, given the flow,\nupslope, and lake assist, this seems unlikely.",
